# ticket.env.example — every figure Gates' copy sale needs, in one place.
#
#   cp ticket.env.example ticket.env   # ticket.env IS gitignored (`*.env`).
#                                      # Put the key in the environment, never here.
#   # rehearse with the EXACT env, no --broadcast — the failure this catches
#   # is a miscounted zero in a price field (TICKET.md §8d):
#   forge script script/DeployGameTicket.s.sol --rpc-url $RPC
#   forge script script/DeployGameTicket.s.sol --rpc-url $RPC --broadcast
#
# The ceremony is docs/store/TICKET.md §8b (eight acts, ordered) and the day
# order is docs/launch/CHECKLIST.md step 8. This file is the figures.
#
# ⚠ PRIVATE_KEY IS NOT IN THIS FILE AND MUST NOT BE ADDED TO IT.
#
# LEGEND:
#   [WELDED]  a constructor argument. No setter exists, at any price.
#   [SETTER]  changeable later by the owner (setPrices / setMetadata / rails).
#   [LOCAL]   read by the script only; changes nothing on chain.
#
# Anything marked <FROM DEPLOYMENTS> is read out of contracts/deployments.json
# on the day, never retyped here — the ticket welds whatever address it is
# given, and hive.env.example already demonstrated how a template staging a
# stale address nearly welds a ceremony to a dead coin.

# ── identity [WELDED] ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THE TITLE AND NOTHING ELSE (operator, 2026-08-12): the contract builds both
# names off it — an item is `Gates #1`, the collection is `Gates on Elo Pros`.
# Typing the platform in here yields "Gates on Elo Pros on Elo Pros", forever.
TICKET_NAME="Gates"
TICKET_SYMBOL="GATES"
TICKET_GAME="gates"

# ── addresses [WELDED] ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The reserve. chains.4663.contracts.ELO — NOT .SCRY, the retired coin.
TICKET_SCRY=<FROM DEPLOYMENTS — ELO, after CHECKLIST step 1>
# The NEW splitter from CHECKLIST step 5. The deployed ScryFeeSplitter welds
# the retired coin; point the ticket at it and the reserve-rail burn is
# unreachable except by rescue().
TICKET_SINK=<FROM DEPLOYMENTS — EloFeeSplitter, after CHECKLIST step 5>
# USDG — the dollar rail's asset. ⭐ SPOKEN 2026-08-21 and READ BACK VERIFIED
# the same day off the explorer: Global Dollar, 6 decimals, the same address
# the x402 rail already uses (meter/rh_facilitator.py). This one is safe to
# stage because it is not ours and does not move with the relaunch.
TICKET_USDG=0x5fc5360D0400a0Fd4f2af552ADD042D716F1d168

# ── the shape [WELDED unless marked] ───────────────────────────────────────
# 0 = uncapped, and 0 is right: the counter bounds free claims AND paid sales,
# so a cap sized for sales gets spent by the free doors and then nobody can
# buy (CHECKLIST step 8).
TICKET_SUPPLY_CAP=0
# Default: the dev wallet. [WELDED]
#TICKET_PROCEEDS=0x...
# Default: the broadcasting key. [SETTER-adjacent: ownership transfers]
#TICKET_OWNER=0x...
# The SITE base, used for external_url only — metadata renders on chain.
TICKET_BASE_URI=https://elopros.com

# ── the opening prices [SETTER — but post them IN the deploy broadcast] ────
# The dollar is the unit of account (SENTENCES.md 2026-08-21): $10, with the
# ETH and USDG rails armed and the reserve rail SHUT (0) on day one. Derive
# the ETH amount from the tape on the day — after the first post,
# `python3 meter/reprice.py --game gates` composes the follow-the-dollar call.
TICKET_PRICE_USD_CENTS=1000
#TICKET_PRICE_WEI=<derive on the day: $10 of ETH, 18 decimals>
TICKET_PRICE_SCRY=0
# $10 of USDG at 6 decimals — parity is exact integer arithmetic, no tape:
TICKET_PRICE_USDG=10000000

# After the broadcast (TICKET.md §8b carries the order):
#   - record the address in deployments.json as EloGameTicket:GATES
#   - SCRY_TICKET_GATES=0x... on the meter — the card and the depot gate light
#     up with no code change
#   - setFreeCollection(<the seat>) and setFreeRoot(<root B>) — CHECKLIST step
#     8b: the ONLY two free doors (2026-08-21)
#   - ⚠ NO COIN LEG: a copy grants no game coin — Gates' pair launches
#     graduated, and the coin-with-copy grant is a curve-phase mechanic
#     (SENTENCES.md 2026-08-21)
